<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN JULY FARM IMPORT VALUE DOWN 23.8 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN JULY FARM IMPORT VALUE DOWN 23.8 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's agricultural imports in July was US$194.9 million, down 23.8 percent from US$255.9 million in July 1996, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the July import decline to slow feed demand in the wake of an islandwide outbreak of hog foot-and-month disease that has rocked the Taiwan's feedlots since late March.</p>
<p>Grains and oilseeds were again the top farm items imported in July.</p>
<p>July import tonnages were not available, but traders estimated that 300,000 tonnes of corn and 50,000 tonnes of soybean arrived at Taiwan ports during July.</p>
<p>Major grain import figures (in millions US$):</p>
<p>			  July 1997	  July 1996</p>
<p> Wheat			 29.8		 38.0</p>
<p> Corn			  57.6		100.4</p>
<p> Soybeans		    24.3		 53.2</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
